Auralayer Privacy Policy

Last updated: May 29, 2026

Auralayer is designed to operate primarily on your device.

Information Collection and Use
Auralayer does not collect, sell, rent, or share personal information through the app.
The app does not require account creation, does not include advertising SDKs, does not use analytics SDKs, and does not transmit usage data to Auralayer servers.

Local Data Storage
Auralayer stores certain app data locally on your device so the app can function properly and restore your listening experience.
This may include saved mixes, presets, selected sounds, music selections, and volume settings.
This locally stored app data is not transmitted by Auralayer to the developer.

Permissions
Auralayer may use Android media playback, foreground service, notification, and related system capabilities to support background audio playback and show playback controls in notifications or on the lock screen.
If notification access is denied, audio playback may still function, but notification-based playback controls may be limited or unavailable depending on Android system behavior.

Support Communications
If you contact support by email, your email address and the contents of your message may be provided through your email provider and received by Auralayer support.
This information is used only to respond to your inquiry.

Data Deletion
Because Auralayer stores app data locally on your device, you can remove this data at any time by clearing the app’s storage or uninstalling the app.

Changes to This Privacy Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time.
If material changes are made, the updated version will be posted with a revised “Last updated” date.

Contact
If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, you may contact:
